{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1076359-2e-maeljins-and-other-preys","id":1076359,"title":"[2E] Maeljins and other Preys","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-11T00:55:50-07:00","id":1076359,"title":"[2E] Maeljins and other Preys","content":"I think that Maeljins can be great chronicle antagonists, on par of Idigam. Especially, as you can connect other Sacred Preys for Tribes of Moon to Lords of Wounds. There is only one I have problem with, so maybe you can help me how to resolve last one antagonists to work for Maeljins. Here is what I have for now in relation to Tribes.<ul><li><b>Blood Talons -</b> <i><b>Werewolves</b></i> - The dreadful <b>Bale Hounds</b>, Uratha cultists of Maeljins, are greatest and most dangerous of their servants.</li> <li><b>Bone Shadows</b> <b>-</b> <i><b>Spirits</b></i> - <b>Maeltinet</b>, commanders and lieutenants of spirits hordes under Lords of Wounds, are alien spirits-like beings living in Wounds in Shadow Realm.</li> <li><b>Iron Masters \u2013 <i>Humans</i> </b>\u2013 The wicked mortal <b>Cults of Great Sins</b>, sacrificing other humans for power , money or lustful desires. Each cult works under one of Maeljin patron.</li> <li><b>Storm Lords \u2013 <i>Claimed</i> </b>\u2013 Lords of Wounds stir many spirits in Shadow Realm, whispering to them to take the ruling in Flesh of weak mortals. Many of them listen to them. Created this way Claimed are</li> </ul><br /> And now we are left only with <b>Hunters in Darkness</b> and <b>Hosts</b> as their Sacred Prey. Hosts are decentralized and generally \u2018they own thing\u2019, so I have problem with reconnecting them to the \u2018Maeljin masters\u2019 in above chronicle scenario. <b>Any idea how Hosts could play in this kind of story?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T01:02:53-07:00","id":1076363,"title":"","content":"Hired muscle is always an option, and some hybrid-stage Hosts engage in cult behavior and exhibit alien faiths that can easily be routed to worship of Sin.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And considering how the Hunters in Darkness in particular are concerned with holy sites in their territory, a loci or some other important place being turned into an Wound will certainly rile them up, whether Hosts are involved or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 04-11-2017, 04:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T02:07:24-07:00","id":1076373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1076359-2e-maeljins-and-other-preys?p=1076363#post1076363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: And considering how the Hunters in Darkness in particular are concerned with holy sites in their territory, a loci or some other important place being turned into an Wound will certainly rile them up, whether Hosts are involved or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Hunters can declare on Sacred Hunt to hunt for 'Those things that desacred our Holy Site into Wound'? Not precise targets?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T02:13:31-07:00","id":1076376,"title":"","content":"Hmm, my memory's shaky. Can the Siskur-Dah only be executed on the Tribal/Lodge's choice of prey? I thought the rite itself can be initiated at any prey, not just the favored prey. Will have to look up again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T02:31:15-07:00","id":1076379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1076359-2e-maeljins-and-other-preys?p=1076376#post1076376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, my memory's shaky. Can the Siskur-Dah only be executed on the Tribal/Lodge's choice of prey? I thought the rite itself can be initiated at any prey, not just the favored prey. Will have to look up again.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can execute it on any prey. But if I rememver correctly, each Tribe (and Lodge) had a unique benefit tied to their respective versions of the rite that was especially potent against their favored prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T02:44:02-07:00","id":1076381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1076359-2e-maeljins-and-other-preys?p=1076379#post1076379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can execute it on any prey. But if I rememver correctly, each Tribe (and Lodge) had a unique benefit tied to their respective versions of the rite that was especially potent against their favored prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was it.<br /> <br /> <br /> So the Hunters in Darkness can and will call the Siskur-Dah on those strange creatures popping out of desecrated loci, whether they know what those things are Shartha or not. Because it's their duty to watch over the holy places, and a Hunt to that end will always be Sacred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  refined 04-11-2017, 05:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T06:37:15-07:00","id":1076444,"title":"","content":"Still, it will be a bit 'unfair' if all other Tribes have their direct Sacred Preys and full bonus on Siskur-Dah Rite on hunting them - and Hunters in Darkness going without this bonus. So how to make Hosts working for Maeljinn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T07:07:24-07:00","id":1076461,"title":"","content":"Just make a Sin Host. You could argue that demons are already this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T01:06:44-07:00","id":1077565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1076359-2e-maeljins-and-other-preys?p=1076461#post1076461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just make a Sin Host. You could argue that demons are already this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are not Possesed more like Claimed, in that they are, well... possesed by demon? Exorcism are, theoretically, working on Inferno Possesed, if I remember 1E book correctly.<br /> <br /> Hosts, on the other hand, are totally merge of Spirit and Flesh, like good old Pangeans. And Hosts are made of animals spirits and flesh, merging with humans. from what I know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-13-2017, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T01:29:44-07:00","id":1077574,"title":"","content":"A Hunter of Darkness sees the current state of the Gauntlet and if it is altered by any origin. My suggestion is, if a Wound appears it definitivly alters the Gauntlet (not in rules but in a cosmetic way) cause the material side becomes influenced. So a Meninna can have full Bonus of Siskur'Dah i would say. Even an enemy can be the reason of this alteration, so a Hunter can see this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/422-lykas","name":"Lykas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar422_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T02:41:03-07:00","id":1077588,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/422-lykas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar422_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"422\" data-vbnamecard=\"422\">Lykas</a> , yeah, 'stink of Wound' for Hunters in Darkness sounds as good way to make them really relevant to Maeljinns workings with Siskur-Dah. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T07:42:13-07:00","id":1077728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1076359-2e-maeljins-and-other-preys?p=1077565#post1077565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hosts, on the other hand, are totally merge of Spirit and Flesh, like good old Pangeans. And Hosts are made of animals spirits and flesh, merging with humans. from what I know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hosts don't have to be limited to animals, and you were asking what the Hunters in Darkness could hunt. Their sacred prey is hosts. So a Sin-host would make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T09:37:11-07:00","id":1077770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1076359-2e-maeljins-and-other-preys?p=1077728#post1077728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a Sin-host would make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>But WHAT would be Sin-Host? You are telling me we have Mountain-Host as there was Pangean like that? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T13:06:50-07:00","id":1077868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1076359-2e-maeljins-and-other-preys?p=1077770#post1077770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But WHAT would be Sin-Host? You are telling me we have Mountain-Host as there was Pangean like that? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>We have fungi hosts too. But the hosts don't seem to be limited to Pangeans. We have the Locust host, for instance, which are likely from an idigam, Mussughana.<br /> <br /> Like I said, a demon could be a sin-host, rebuilding themselves to become the Adversary. Or you could just pick a sin and go with it. Gluttony hosts people with an insatiable appetite, who seek out others with the same and have powers similar to the Gluttony investments.<br /> <br /> There's a ton of ways you could go with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T14:48:01-07:00","id":1077935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1076359-2e-maeljins-and-other-preys?p=1077868#post1077868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We have fungi hosts too. But the hosts don't seem to be limited to Pangeans. We have the Locust host, for instance, which are likely from an idigam, Mussughana.<br /> <br /> Like I said, a demon could be a sin-host, rebuilding themselves to become the Adversary. Or you could just pick a sin and go with it. Gluttony hosts people with an insatiable appetite, who seek out others with the same and have powers similar to the Gluttony investments.<br /> <br /> There's a ton of ways you could go with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds so wonderfully messed up and has just the thing a high-end woof game needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T18:24:20-07:00","id":1078067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1076359-2e-maeljins-and-other-preys?p=1077770#post1077770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But WHAT would be Sin-Host?</div> </div> </div> </div>Check out the Uglathlu on pages 122-7 of Night Horrors: Wolfsbane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T17:50:23-07:00","id":1079588,"title":"","content":"You could go with Maggot Hosts, a type of Host that hide from the Forsaken in Wounds and were eventually corrupted into servants of sin. <br /> <br /> Maggots and Wounds fit together thematically anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T18:53:04-07:00","id":1079614,"title":"","content":"Honestly, there's no need to even bother trying to do the association of Host to Maelin. The reasons why HiD have Hosts as their prey (from an IC standpoint anyways) is that their Siskur-Dah makes them highly suited from discovering the Hosts' lairs. <br /> <br /> &quot;The Hunter in Darkness Sacred Hunt grants your character the ability to sense the state of the Gauntlet in your presence; you are constantly aware of its current strength and if it has been increased or decreased compared to its normal strength; if the hunt\u2019s prey is responsible then you know this. You can also sense any other breaches in reality that your prey has moved through in the last lunar month \u2014 gateways to places and realms other than the Shadow.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sharatha mess with the gauntlet. That's their calling card. Don't worry about creating new Hosts when the current ability works perfectly fine for finding Wounds. Even if you made &quot;inferno Hosts,&quot; if they're not messing with the gauntlet, then its utterly meaningless. And, lets not forget that Wounds are sucking holes to the Inferno in the first place, so they're already falling under the Siskur-Dah's benefit. Locating the heart of a Wound is a pretty nice benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T20:17:22-07:00","id":1079651,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2241\" data-vbnamecard=\"2241\">Omegaphallic</a>, Setchel pointed me exactly to them. And now I agree. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1076359-2e-maeljins-and-other-preys?p=1078067#post1078067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Check out the Uglathlu on pages 122-7 of Night Horrors: Wolfsbane.</div> </div> </div> </div> Holy crap, I want to use them sooo much! I only have setting limitatios - city we will run is only like 150 thousands citizens - that does not sound enought to have any mafia family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T20:28:46-07:00","id":1079658,"title":"","content":"While the specific Mafia family can be excised, they can invade anyone with poor moral fiber. And there's bound to be someone like that in a town that large.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T20:46:36-07:00","id":1079664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1076359-2e-maeljins-and-other-preys?p=1079658#post1079658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the specific Mafia family can be excised, they can invade anyone with poor moral fiber. And there's bound to be someone like that in a town that large.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that mafia family probably no - but a gang or two of thieves and extortions. PCs will probably run one of those themselves. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T04:38:01-07:00","id":1080820,"title":"","content":"Maybe Maeljin can affect some hosts? Some swarms of Infernal Azlu or Abyssal Beshilu, who imbued the mark of Maeljin to be more effective in their agenda (which too a bit changes, representing Maeljin interests)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid"